about_content_=Everyone knows that women naturally have a higher body fat percentage than men. This means that women also have a higher fat content in their brains, which explains why it is universally acknowledged around the world that women are less intelligent than men.<br/><br/>Tens of thousands of years ago, although humanity had not yet acquired the relevant specialized knowledge, wise men had already deduced the root cause of this difference through physical exploration and contemplation. They named it the Damping Effect. Ever since then, people have tactfully described women as: animals driven by instinct.<br/><br/>In modern times, top transgender scientists from the fields of biology and neuroscience around the world joined forces to overturn this absurd theory. They established a nonprofit organization called the Anti-Sexism Association and, sparing no expense, recruited thousands of volunteers for live human dissection experiments. Eventually, the scientists reached a conclusion: in a non-dehydrated state, the vast majority of the human brain's structure is composed of fat. Regardless of age or sex, whether an infant or an elderly person, the fat percentage of the human brain is a constant 63%.<br/><br/>These findings debunked the stereotype that humanity had held for tens of thousands of years: that the root cause of women's lower intelligence was their higher fat percentage. Data defeated ignorance. Science defeated common sense.<br/><br/>As we can see, women simply have a higher fat percentage in certain parts of their bodies, while the fat percentage in their brains is exactly the same as men's. Fat percentage is not the reason women have lower intelligence. It must be caused by something else.
